Said BOUDJELDA created KAFKA-20113:
--------------------------------------

             Summary: Add Configurable Retry Parameters for Status Backing =
Store
                 Key: KAFKA-20113
                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-20113
             Project: Kafka
          Issue Type: New Feature
          Components: connect
            Reporter: Said BOUDJELDA
            Assignee: Said BOUDJELDA
             Fix For: 4.2.0


Implement configurable retry parameters for the +KafkaStatusBackingStore+
to address the TODO comment "retry more gracefully and not forever" and pro=
vide operators with control over retry behavior during transient failures.
h3. Problem Statement
=C2=A0
KafkaStatusBackingStore=C2=A0currently retries status updates indefinitely =
when encountering retriable exceptions. This behavior is problematic becaus=
e:
 # *Infinite retry loops*=C2=A0can cause the worker to become unresponsive =
during extended Kafka broker outages
 # *No visibility*=C2=A0into retry behavior - operators cannot tune retry p=
arameters based on their environment
 # *Resource exhaustion*=C2=A0- indefinite retries can consume threads and =
memory during prolonged failures
 # *No graceful degradation*=C2=A0- the system continues retrying without b=
ound rather than failing fast when appropriate

A TODO comment in the codebase ({{{}// TODO: retry more gracefully and not =
forever{}}}) explicitly acknowledges this issue needs addressing.
h3. Proposed Solution

Add four new configuration properties under the=C2=A0{{status.storage.}}=C2=
=A0prefix to control retry behavior:

=C2=A0
||Property||Type||Default||Description||
|{{status.storage.retry.max.retries}}|INT|5|Maximum number of retry attempt=
s before giving up|
|{{status.storage.retry.initial.backoff.ms}}|LONG|300|Initial backoff delay=
 in milliseconds|
|{{status.storage.retry.max.backoff.ms}}|LONG|10000|Maximum backoff delay c=
ap in milliseconds|
|{{status.storage.retry.backoff.multiplier}}|DOUBLE|2.0|Multiplier applied =
to backoff after each attempt|

The retry mechanism uses=C2=A0*exponential backoff with jitter*=C2=A0to pre=
vent thundering herd problems during cluster recovery.
h4. Behavior
 * Retries occur only for exceptions marked as=C2=A0{{RetriableException}}
 * After exhausting=C2=A0{{{}max.retries{}}}, the operation logs an error a=
nd terminates gracefully
 * All retry attempts are logged at WARN level with attempt count and delay=
 information
 * Non-retriable exceptions fail immediately without retry
 * =C2=A0

h3. Benefits
 # *Predictable failure modes*=C2=A0- Workers eventually give up and surfac=
e errors instead of hanging
 # *Operator control*=C2=A0- Tune retry behavior based on environment chara=
cteristics
 # *Better observability*=C2=A0- Clear logging of retry attempts and outcom=
es
 # *Backward compatible*=C2=A0- Default values maintain similar behavior to=
 current implementation

=C2=A0

=C2=A0



