Hi Luke and  Kamal:

Thank you for your thorough review, thoughtful discussion, and your vote on
the KIP.

Hi All:
Sorry to bother you, but this KIP still needs one more vote to pass.
I know this is a niche area and not many people are working on it, but I=E2=
=80=99d
still like to reach out. If you have time, I=E2=80=99d really appreciate yo=
ur help
review for this KIP.
Thank you very much.

Regards
Jian

Kamal Chandraprakash <kamal.chandraprakash@gmail.com> =E4=BA=8E2026=E5=B9=
=B42=E6=9C=883=E6=97=A5=E5=91=A8=E4=BA=8C 16:57=E5=86=99=E9=81=93=EF=BC=9A

> Hi Jian,
>
> +1 (binding). Thanks for the KIP!
>
> Thanks,
> Kamal
>
> On Fri, Jan 23, 2026 at 11:47=E2=80=AFAM Luke Chen <showuon@gmail.com> wr=
ote:
>
> > Hi Jian,
> >
> > +1 (binding) from me.
> >
> > Thank you.
> > Luke
> >
> > On Mon, Jan 12, 2026 at 10:13=E2=80=AFPM jian fu <fujian1115@gmail.com>=
 wrote:
> >
> > > Hi all:
> > >
> > > I would like to start a vote for the KIP:
> > >
> > > The KIP: https://cwiki.apache.org/confluence/x/A4LMFw
> > > The Draft PR: https://github.com/apache/kafka/pull/20913
> > >
> > > Summary:
> > >
> > > Currently, Kafka's tiered storage implementation uploads all non-acti=
ve
> > > local log segments to remote storage immediately, even when they are
> > still
> > > within the local retention period.
> > > This results in redundant storage of the same data in both local and
> > remote
> > > which don't have real value in some cases.
> > > This KIP's goal is to reduce the remote storage as an optional topic
> > > feature which can be implemented with few code lines.
> > >
> > > Thanks.
> > > Jian
> > >
> >
