Hi everyone,

Bumping this thread again. I know we're in the middle of the 4.0.2/4.1.2
code freezes and the 4.2 stabilization crunch, but I=E2=80=99d appreciate a=
n
initial look at KIP-1267 when things settle down.

The motivation is solving the visibility gap for remote fetch costs. In
multi-tenant environments, we can't currently attribute S3/GCS egress to
specific consumers because metrics are only at the topic level. This makes
chargeback and identifying "noisy neighbors" a pain for anyone running
tiered storage at scale.

Satish, Harsha, Josep =E2=80=94 given your work on KIP-405, I=E2=80=99d spe=
cifically value
your take on adding client-id tags to the RemoteLogManager. Also interested
in whether we should align these with the OpenTelemetry/KIP-714 standards
or stick to standard JMX tags.

KIP:
https://cwiki.apache.org/confluence/display/KAFKA/KIP-1267%3A+Tiered+Storag=
e+Cost+Attribution+Metrics


Jira: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-20047

Regards,

Viquar khan

https://www.linkedin.com/in/vaquar-khan-b695577/

