Hello,

The Call For Papers is now open for the Apache Software Foundation's Commun=
ity Over Code conference this October in Glasgow.

There is a track on "AI Plumbing" at the conference that may be of interest=
 to recipients of this email.

Though it doesn't need to be the plumbing focus, I think that a lot can be =
said about agentic AI.  Agentic AI has gotten a lot of buzz in the AI world=
, and one of the most important things in making agents useful is throwing =
them together with some good plumbing, e.g. linear or graph-based workflows=
, orchestration tactics, -communication- protocols, memory, knowledge graph=
s, etc.  There is a lot to talk about.  This track might be a perfect place=
 to present efforts in the area, display some work, and perhaps hold a gene=
ral discussion on experience.

Again, Agentic AI is not the focus.  Anything regarding putting together an=
y type of AI workflows will be considered relevant.

Please forward this email to anybody you know that might be interested in t=
he Community Over Code 2026 conference and may not have received this email=
.

The home page for Community Over Code 2026: https://communityovercode.org/


Thank you for reading,

Sean Finan
Apache cTAKES









Sean Finan
Research Computing Principal Engineer
Computational Health Informatics Program (CHIP), Natural Language Processin=
g Lab
