Hey Chia,

this is mentioned in the KIP, albeit well hidden: "Where, for simplicity,
we can assume the assignment epoch of a partition that is not assigned to
that member to be Integer.maxValue.". Although I realize now that this
explanation suffers from an off-by-one error, so let me put it this way:

You cannot commit partitions that are not assigned to you.

Hope that clarifies it.

Cheers
Lucas

