Subject: [VOTE] KIP-1274: Deprecate and remove support for Classic rebalance
 protocol in KafkaConsumer
To: dev@kafka.apache.org
Content-Type: multipart/alternative; boundary="000000000000d9f130064b070a36"
From: Lianet Magrans <lianetm@apache.org>
Reply-To: <dev@kafka.apache.org>

--000000000000d9f130064b070a36
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="UTF-8"

Hi all,

I would like to start a vote on KIP-1274 that proposes a path towards the
deprecation and removal of the Classic rebalance protocol in the
KafkaConsumer.

The KIP proposes a phased long-term plan, starting with recommendations to
upgrade to the generally available Consumer protocol, and having the main
deprecation and removal changes taking place in the next major releases.

KIP:
https://cwiki.apache.org/confluence/display/KAFKA/KIP-1274%3A+Deprecate+and+remove+support+for+Classic+rebalance+protocol+in+KafkaConsumer

Discussion thread:
https://lists.apache.org/thread/9qg8zkv8jb9y16hl578w4b619yqk9pdo

Thanks,
Lianet

--000000000000d9f130064b070a36--

