Hi Jun,

Your question is spot on.

If the MV approach is implemented, a configuration like segment.bytes could h=
ave multiple lower bounds. For instance: an absolute minimum of 1MB, a 2MB bo=
und for MV 4.3, and a 3MB bound for MV 4.7.

During broker startup, if the MV is momentarily unknown, the absolute minimum=
 (1MB) will be applied for validation.

If users have segment.bytes=3D1.5MB in their static files and are just upgrad=
ing the binaries, it will work fine. Since the MV hasn't been bumped yet, the=
 active lower bound remains 1MB.

Later, if users try to update the MV from 4.2 to 4.3, the validation will use=
 the new 2MB lower bound, causing the MV upgrade to fail. To proceed, users m=
ust update the configs dynamically to at least 2MB (which overrides the stati=
c config) before they can successfully bump the MV.

Best,
Chia-Ping

