> Move logic for state store initiation to StreamThread handover
> --------------------------------------------------------------
>
>                 Key: KAFKA-19434
>                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-19434
>             Project: Kafka
>          Issue Type: Task
>          Components: streams
>            Reporter: Bill Bejeck
>            Assignee: Eduwer Camacaro
>            Priority: Blocker
>
> When starting a Kafka Streams instance, if it has pre-existing state, the=
 state stores are initialized on the main thread. Part of this
> initialization registers the stateful metrics with the JMX thread-id tag =
of=C2=A0{{{}main{}}}. This breaks the KIP-1076 implementation where need to
> register metrics with thread-id tags of=C2=A0{{{}xxxStreamThread-N{}}}. T=
his is necessary due to the fact that the=C2=A0{{StreamsMetric}}=C2=A0is a =
singleton shared
> by all=C2=A0{{StreamThread}} instances, so we need to make sure only add =
metrics for the current=C2=A0{{StreamThread}}=C2=A0otherwise duplicate metr=
ics are
> registered.=C2=A0 So the task is to move state store initialization to th=
e point when the main thread hands the store over to the assigned `StreamTh=
read`



