Hey folks,

We here at LinkedIn are on our journey to move to Northguard and as such ou=
r participation with Apache Kafka has lessened over the years. Despite not =
actively contributing to Kafka anymore, we have developed and maintained Ka=
fka Cruise Control and made it available to the community which has gained =
wide adoption across the users of Kafka.

As we move further towards full Northguard adoption and our Kafka footprint=
 shrinks, we also have made less investment in the Cruise Control project a=
s well. However, we don't want to let the project die within LinkedIn and f=
orce a community fork. As such, we want to investigate relieving ourselves =
of ownership and donating Cruise Control. We believe Apache Kafka is likely=
 the right spot for this overall to maintain close continuity with the core=
 Kafka project.

We'd like to begin a conversation on this and discuss what the process woul=
d look like compared to other open source options. We have had discussions =
in the past with Linux Foundation as well. If you could help identify who'd=
 be the right contact to start discussions with, I'd appreciate it!

Thanks,

Krit Petty,
Sr. Manager, Kafka, LinkedIn


