Hello Siddhartha,

Thanks for this KIP. Wanted to catch up on it for a long time... Overall 
the KIP make sense to me. Two comments:

MJS1: While I agree that we should put the helpers into an internal 
package, I don't think we can move them -- we would rather need to 
duplicate them, and mark the current ones as deprecated for now and 
remove them only in 5.0 release. Even if it's very unlikely that users 
would rely on these helpers, we should not just move them to internal 
packages and potentially break user code.


MJS2: About `Time` -- looking forward to a follow up KIP. In 
KafkaStreams we only use `Time` for testing, so it make sense to 
deprecate the corresponding constructors IMHO. -- Later on, ie, AK 5.0 
release, I believe the right way to handle it would be to make these 
constructors package private and add a new `KafkaStreamsMock` sub-class 
(or similar) in our testing code to still allow us to pass in a mock time.


-Matthias



