Hi Matthias,

Thank you for the feedback. I appreciate you taking the time to review this=
.

MJS1 - Helper methods deprecation:

You are right about maintaining backward compatibility. I have updated the
KIP to follow the proper deprecation path:


   - Helper methods will remain in their current location but be marked as =
d
   eprecated
   - Duplicate helpers will be added in
   "org.apache.kafka.common.utils.internals.BytesUtils" for internal Kafka =
use
   - The deprecated public helpers will be removed only in version 5.0

This ensures we don't break any existing user code, however unlikely the
usage might be.

MJS2 - Time API:

Agreed. I will work on a separate KIP for the Time API. Your suggestion
about deprecating the KafkaStreams constructors that accept "Time" and
eventually using a KafkaStreamsMock approach makes sense.

Here is the updated KIP:
https://cwiki.apache.org/confluence/display/KAFKA/KIP-1247%3A+Make+Bytes+ut=
ils+class+part+of+the+public+API

Please let me know if the updated KIP addresses your concerns.

Best regards,
Siddhartha


On Sun, Feb 22, 2026 at 8:27=E2=80=AFPM Matthias J. Sax <mjsax@apache.org> =
wrote:

> Hello Siddhartha,
>
> Thanks for this KIP. Wanted to catch up on it for a long time... Overall
> the KIP make sense to me. Two comments:
>
> MJS1: While I agree that we should put the helpers into an internal
> package, I don't think we can move them -- we would rather need to
> duplicate them, and mark the current ones as deprecated for now and
> remove them only in 5.0 release. Even if it's very unlikely that users
> would rely on these helpers, we should not just move them to internal
> packages and potentially break user code.
>
>
> MJS2: About `Time` -- looking forward to a follow up KIP. In
> KafkaStreams we only use `Time` for testing, so it make sense to
> deprecate the corresponding constructors IMHO. -- Later on, ie, AK 5.0
> release, I believe the right way to handle it would be to make these
> constructors package private and add a new `KafkaStreamsMock` sub-class
> (or similar) in our testing code to still allow us to pass in a mock time=
.
>
>
> -Matthias
>
>
>
> On 12/29/25 9:48 AM, Siddhartha Devineni wrote:
> > Hi all,
> >
> > (Apologies for posting this mistakenly in a separate thread - resending
> > here to keep the discussion organized)
> >
> > I have updated the KIP-1247 based on feedback from Chia-Ping.
> >
> > Key changes:
> >
> >     - The KIP now proposes to make only the core *Bytes* methods
> officially
> >     public (Bytes, wrap, get, compareTo, equals, hashCode, toString)
> >     - Helper methods/fields (increment(), ByteArrayComparator,
> >     BYTES_LEXICO_COMPARATOR) will be moved to
> >     "org.apache.kafka.common.utils.internals package"
> >     - This approach keeps the public API minimal while allowing interna=
l
> >     Kafka code to continue using the helpers
> >
> > Updated KIP:
> >
> https://cwiki.apache.org/confluence/display/KAFKA/KIP-1247%3A+Make+Bytes+=
utils+class+part+of+the+public+API
> >
> > Please review the changes and let me know if you have any concerns. If
> > there are no objections in the next few days, then I would like to call
> for
> > a vote.
> >
> > Thank you.
> >
> > Best regards,
> > Siddhartha
> >
> >
> > On Mon, Dec 29, 2025 at 12:17=E2=80=AFAM Siddhartha Devineni <
> > siddhartha.devineni@gmail.com> wrote:
> >
> >> Hi Chia-Ping,
> >>
> >> My apologies for the confusion, as I misunderstood your suggestion.
> >>
> >> You were suggesting moving helpers like increment(),
> ByteArrayComparator,
> >> and BYTES_LEXICO_COMPARATOR to the
> >> "org.apache.kafka.common.utils.internals" package while keeping them
> public
> >> in Java visibility terms so that they can have their current
> >> characteristics such as the other internal packages can use them, they
> are
> >> not exposed to the users and no burden of maintaining them for backwar=
d
> >> compatilibility.
> >>
> >> This is a much cleaner approach. I will update the KIP to reflect thes=
e:
> >>
> >> 1. Make only the core Bytes methods (Bytes, wrap, get, compareTo,
> equals,
> >> hashCode, toString) officially part of the public API
> >> 2. Move the helper methods/fields to
> >> "org.apache.kafka.common.utils.internals"
> >>
> >> Thank you for your patience in explaining this.
> >>
> >> Best regards,
