Hello team,
In this discussion thread we will finalise the design for the KIP-1289 Supp=
ort Hierarchical Transactional Acknowledgments for Share Groups.=C2=A0

Share Groups currently support only immediate acknowledgement modes (IMPLIC=
IT/EXPLICIT). This causes data loss in distributed streaming frameworks:

1. Worker acknowledges records =E2=86=92 Records removed from Kafka
2. Checkpoint fails before sink write
3. Records lost (acknowledged but never persisted)

Goal: Enable exactly-once read semantics via transactional acknowledgements=
.
We already have similar pattern in Kafka producer transaction

KIP:=C2=A0KIP-1289 Support Hierarchical Transactional Acknowledgments for S=
hare Groups - Apache Kafka - Apache Software Foundation=C2=A0

Looking forward to community's feedback!=C2=A0


Regards,Shekhar Prasad Rajak


