>                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-10686
>             Project: Kafka
>          Issue Type: New Feature
>          Components: streams
>            Reporter: Levani Kokhreidze
>            Priority: Major
>              Labels: needs-kip
>
> In production, Kafka Streams instances often run across different cluster=
s and availability zones. In order to guarantee high availability of the Ka=
fka Streams deployments, users would need more granular control over which =
instances standby tasks can be created.=C2=A0
> Idea of this ticket is to expose interface for Kafka Streams which can be=
 implemented by the users to control where standby tasks can be created.
> Kafka Streams can have RackAware assignment as a default implementation t=
hat will take into account `rack.id` of the application and make sure that =
standby tasks are created on different racks.=C2=A0
> Point of this ticket though is to give more flexibility to users on stand=
by task creation, in cases where just rack awareness is not enough.=C2=A0



