Hi Sean,

Thanks for your question.

Currently, the Admin interface provides alter offsets and delete offsets =
APIs=20
that can be used to "reset" a consumer group's offsets.=20
At the moment, these APIs require the group to be inactive.
With the new pause implementation, we will relax this requirement. The =
new flow will look like this:
    =E2=80=A2 The consumer group is active.
    =E2=80=A2 The pause partitions API is invoked.
    =E2=80=A2 The group coordinator eventually unassigns those =
partitions.=20
       Until this happens, the offset commit API will return an error=20
       for any requests coming from the Admin API.
    =E2=80=A2 Once the partitions are "paused" and no longer assigned to =
a member,=20
      the validation in both Streams and the=20
      modern group implementation will recognize this and allow the =
offset commit to succeed.
The flow for CLI tools will be similar. In short, the Admin API will =
return an=20
error until the consumer successfully reconciles with the paused =
partitions.

Hope this answers your question!

Thanks,
Levani

