highluck created KAFKA-20234:
--------------------------------

             Summary: Replace System.out.println with proper logger for mis=
sing property file warning
                 Key: KAFKA-20234
                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-20234
             Project: Kafka
          Issue Type: Improvement
            Reporter: highluck
            Assignee: highluck


=C2=A0 Currently, when a property file is not specified, the message "Did n=
ot load any properties since the property file is not specified" is printed=
 using =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0=C2=A0
=C2=A0 System.out.println. This is inconsistent with the rest of the codeba=
se, which uses SLF4J logging.

=C2=A0 Replace System.out.println with log.warn to ensure consistent loggin=
g behavior and allow proper log level filtering and output control.



--
